 and enforced key-only SSH authentication, then restarted node1 and verified the configuration survived reboot.\",\"actions_performed\":[\"Created opsadmin user on node1 (useradd -m)\",\"Installed ~/.ssh (700) with authorized_keys (600) containing the exact required ed25519 public key\",\"Locked opsadmin's password (passwd -l) so no password credential exists\",\"Added /etc/ssh/sshd_config.d/60-key-only.conf setting PubkeyAuthentication yes, PasswordAuthentication no, KbdInteractiveAuthentication no, ChallengeResponseAuthentication no\",\"Validated sshd config syntax (sshd -t) and reloaded sshd\",\"Functionally verified via a temporary throwaway keypair that pubkey login succeeds and password login is rejected, then removed the throwaway key leaving only the required key\",\"Captured pre-restart baseline (boot_id, uptime -s, sshd active, effective sshd -T settings, opsadmin shadow entry)\",\"Issued systemctl reboot on node1 via backgrounded nohup so the ack returned before disconnect\",\"Polled node1 until exec succeeded again\",\"Confirmed boot_id and uptime -s changed, proving an actual restart occurred\",\"Re-verified post-reboot: sshd active with same key-only settings persisted, opsadmin password still locked, authorized_keys still contains only the required key\",\"Ran a second temporary-key functional test post-reboot confirming pubkey login works and password login is refused, then cleaned up the temporary key\"],\"evidence\":[{\"requirement\":\"opsadmin user created with the exact required SSH public key in authorized_keys\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-ef759466ad134055\",\"cmd-72f4fd746b1f40ae\"],\"summary\":\"useradd created opsadmin (uid 1000); authorized_keys populated and verified to contain exactly the requested ed25519 key with correct 700/600 permissions\"},{\"requirement\":\"SSH authentication restricted to key-based only\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-3e17218323ea46e3\",\"cmd-38ae4fa3471f4756\"],\"summary\":\"Drop-in sshd config written and syntax-validated (